    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-1-1-3",
      "sourceStart": 1137,
      "sourceEnd": 1267,
      "original": "#### 1.1.3. <span style=\"color: red\">(Self-adjoint) </span>An operator $T\\in\\mathcal{L}(V)$ is called **self-adjoint** if $T=T^*$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
