      "sourceStart": 8516,
      "sourceEnd": 8580,
      "original": "### 2.4. Isometrics, Unitary Operators, and Matrix Factorization",
      "action": "moved-to-section-title"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0037",
      "sourceStart": 8580,
      "sourceEnd": 8582,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-4-1",
      "sourceStart": 8582,
      "sourceEnd": 8731,
      "original": "#### 2.4.1. Suppose $V,W$ are finite-dimensional inner product spaces and let $S \\in \\mathcal{L}(V,W)$. Then the following statements are equivalent.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0038",
      "sourceStart": 8731,
      "sourceEnd": 9144,
      "sha256": "ee8ee64150121532ac0e8cbb5e5d2bf2afa7f76b695b4d1c83e487435f7c45ad"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-4-2",
      "sourceStart": 9144,
      "sourceEnd": 9340,
      "original": "#### 2.4.2. Suppose $V$ is a finite-dimensional inner product space with an orthonormal basis $\\beta=\\{e_1,\\ldots,e_n\\}$ and let $S\\in\\mathcal{L}(V)$. Then the following statements are equivalent.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0039",
      "sourceStart": 9340,
      "sourceEnd": 9630,
      "sha256": "baef943cd6a90ae9ae2783995d9e722f2ca83ed5d6b66264e5229319dcd3208a"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-4-3",
      "sourceStart": 9630,
      "sourceEnd": 9738,
      "original": "#### 2.4.3. Suppose $F=\\mathbb{C}$ and $S \\in \\mathcal{L}(V)$. Then the following statements are equivalent.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0040",
      "sourceStart": 9738,
      "sourceEnd": 9906,
      "sha256": "5e78c39fc992d556d860f76ec155d420745e4f9725ce1b3f60802603db92ea05"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-4-4",
      "sourceStart": 9906,
      "sourceEnd": 9995,
      "original": "#### 2.4.4. Suppose $Q \\in F^{n \\times n}$. Then the following statements are equivalent.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0041",
      "sourceStart": 9995,
      "sourceEnd": 10143,
      "sha256": "d044cb41559f0d7f760b1f9e929871b82d132f8a76201aab1c2848916926b103"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-4-5",
      "sourceStart": 10143,
      "sourceEnd": 10408,
      "original": "#### 2.4.5. <span style=\"color: red\">(QR factorization)</span> Suppose $A\\in F^{n\\times n}$ has linearly independent columns. Then there exist unique matrices $Q\\text{(unitary)},R\\text{(upper triangular with positive diagonal entries)} \\in F^{n \\times n}$ such that",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0042",
      "sourceStart": 10408,
      "sourceEnd": 10519,
      "sha256": "43008d2f3cfb6c036cae0b3fc330a24b3a1d5ae8e7abc81c4d5d3885900fb2a8"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-4-6",
      "sourceStart": 10519,
      "sourceEnd": 10738,
      "original": "#### 2.4.6. <span style=\"color: red\">(Cholesky factorization)</span> Suppose $B$ is a positive definite matrix. Then there exists a unique upper-triangular matrix $R$ with only positive numbers on its diagonal such that",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0043",
      "sourceStart": 10738,
      "sourceEnd": 10755,
      "sha256": "55485b45ac005045864e3ea4725ab08814fce166f4641f46775f95314bbcf718"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-section-2-5",
      "sourceStart": 10755,
      "sourceEnd": 10792,
      "original": "### 2.5. Singular Value Decomposition",
      "action": "moved-to-section-title"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0044",
      "sourceStart": 10792,
      "sourceEnd": 10794,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-5-1",
      "sourceStart": 10794,
      "sourceEnd": 10844,
      "original": "#### 2.5.1. Suppose $T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V,W)$. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0045",
      "sourceStart": 10844,
      "sourceEnd": 11071,
      "sha256": "36713408f8aac5e6f3e60d1cc45879b2fa49e54c570803b8d40172966c346351"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-5-2",
      "sourceStart": 11071,
      "sourceEnd": 11121,
      "original": "#### 2.5.2. Suppose $T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V,W)$. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0046",
      "sourceStart": 11121,
      "sourceEnd": 11429,
      "sha256": "a2d8f17b4b7e59f9212c21421daa09eea4732a01043fe5175e50c8f68d12f3c3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-5-3",
      "sourceStart": 11429,
      "sourceEnd": 11745,
      "original": "#### 2.5.3. <span style=\"color: red\">(Singular value decomposition)</span> Suppose $T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V,W)$ and the positive singular values of $T$ are $s_1,\\ldots,s_m$, counted with multiplicity ($m=\\operatorname{rank}T$). Then there exist orthonormal lists $e_1,\\ldots,e_m$ in $V$ and $f_1,\\ldots,f_m$ in $W$ where",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0047",
      "sourceStart": 11745,
      "sourceEnd": 12151,
      "sha256": "82c4f8006a62e813606768f25de6b3a9f679290bc8e142440c1d8e7410ead24b"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-5-4",
      "sourceStart": 12151,
      "sourceEnd": 12454,
      "original": "#### 2.5.4. <span style=\"color: red\">(SVD for matrix)</span> Suppose $A \\in F^{p \\times n}$ of rank $m \\geq 1$. Then there exist $B \\in F^{p \\times m}$ with orthonormal columns, a diagonal matrix with positive entries $D \\in F^{m \\times m}$, and $C \\in F^{n \\times m}$ with orthonormal columns such that",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0048",
      "sourceStart": 12454,
      "sourceEnd": 12472,
      "sha256": "4d921fd70da2ca9e51b3fbefbca1f8a51c4d2bae82fd5f9ceb92af40e24e9087"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-section-2-6",
      "sourceStart": 12472,
      "sourceEnd": 12525,
      "original": "### 2.6. Consequences of Singular Value Decomposition",
      "action": "moved-to-section-title"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0049",
      "sourceStart": 12525,
      "sourceEnd": 12527,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-6-1",
      "sourceStart": 12527,
      "sourceEnd": 12625,
      "original": "#### 2.6.1. Suppose $T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V,W)$. Let $s_1$ be the largest singular value of $T$. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0050",
      "sourceStart": 12625,
      "sourceEnd": 12767,
      "sha256": "c317853bdfc9d5dc693428060ab545778dfacd383f5abf1256fd5d135293f732"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-6-2",
      "sourceStart": 12767,
      "sourceEnd": 12819,
      "original": "#### 2.6.2. Suppose $S,T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V,W)$. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0051",
      "sourceStart": 12819,
      "sourceEnd": 12980,
      "sha256": "e485a25d160d544e498e9cace880fc8013cb6d26374600905d851c8d222832cd"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-6-3",
      "sourceStart": 12980,
      "sourceEnd": 13216,
      "original": "#### 2.6.3. Suppose $T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V,W)$ and $s_1 \\geq \\cdots \\geq s_m$ are the positive singular values of $T$ with corresponding orthonormal vectors $e_1,\\ldots,e_m$ in $V$ and $f_1,\\ldots,f_m$ in $W$. Suppose $1 \\leq k < m$. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch07-block-0052",
      "sourceStart": 13216,
      "sourceEnd": 13490,
      "sha256": "bf9e994ca6195e04ae0eb80185d494231568003d872f0805fd804ca2582a190a"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch07-item-2-6-4",
      "sourceStart": 13490,
      "sourceEnd": 13603,
      "original": "#### 2.6.4. Suppose $T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V)$. Then there exists a unitary operator $S \\in \\mathcal{L}(V)$ such that",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
